E["item:hand-of-dextren-ward"] = {t="item",n="Hand of Dextren Ward",z="stockade",s="Darkshire demands proof that Dextren Ward has been executed in the Stormwind Stockade. The severed hand is bound for town, where grieving families await justice for their dead.",h="Darkshire demands proof that Dextren Ward has been executed in the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="A Defiler's Toll",b="Dextren Ward was sentenced to death by Lord Ebonlocke after he was caught digging up bodies in Duskwood cemeteries and selling them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Stormwind intervened before the town could execute him and took him to the Stockade. For Darkshire's grieving families, Ward's hand proves the defiler has been executed, despite the House of Nobles' unwanted leniency.",sp=0},{t="A Message to the Nobles",b="Councilman Millstipe's demand for Ward's severed hand also defies the crown. Duskwood feels abandoned by Stormwind's elite, who withhold military aid while asserting their authority when it suits them. Executing a prisoner in the capital's deepest dungeon and claiming his hand tells the House of Nobles that the Darkshire Council will enforce its own laws when the nobles fail them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Dextren Ward?",a="Dextren Ward was caught unearthing corpses from Darkshire's graveyards and selling them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Duskwood sentenced him to beheading, but Stormwind authorities took him to the Stockade instead of carrying out the execution.",al={"dextren ward lore","who is dextren ward","ward crime"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Darkshire want his hand?",a="Councilman Millstipe demands Ward's severed hand as proof of his assassination. It brings closure to the families whose ancestors' graves were plundered and tells the House of Nobles that Darkshire's justice cannot be overridden.",al={"why severed hand","why cut off ward hand","millstipe proof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the Hand of Dextren Ward found?",a="The hand is claimed directly from Dextren Ward in the deeper chambers on the left side of the Stormwind Stockade. He fights as a warrior and has a frightening shout that sends foes fleeing.",al={"where to find ward","stockade ward location","dextren ward location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why did Stormwind imprison Ward instead of executing him?",a="The House of Nobles claimed jurisdiction over Ward and imprisoned him in the Stockade instead of allowing Darkshire to carry out its death sentence. Darkshire's leaders see this as corrupt interference that disregards the frontier town's plight.",al={"why was ward spared","stormwind house of nobles ward","ward imprisoned"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Hand of Dextren Ward?",a="It is the severed hand of Dextren Ward, a notorious grave robber and defiler of the dead who was caught selling corpses from Darkshire's cemetery to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Taken as physical proof of his assassination inside the Stormwind Stockade, it serves as grim confirmation that Lord Ebonlocke's death sentence has finally been carried out.",al={"what is hand of dextren ward","hand of dextren ward item","dextren ward hand"},it="identity",add="48b9455f"},{q="Where does the Hand of Dextren Ward come from?",a="It comes directly from the body of Dextren Ward, severed by your own blade inside his cell at the Stormwind Stockade. Rather than being forged or crafted, it is taken as an irrefutable trophy of justice to be delivered back to Councilman Millstipe in Duskwood.",al={"where did dextren ward hand come from","who made dextren wards hand","origin of hand of dextren ward"},it="origin",add="b59a9a35"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Ward's imprisonment exposes the deep rift between Stormwind's distant House of Nobles and Duskwood's abandoned frontier settlers.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you know Ward was no spellcaster. The bodies he dug up fed Morbent Fel's dark arts, so Ward's death strikes at those who traffic with the dead."},kw={"darkshire","dextren ward","duskwood","ebonlocke","hand of dextren ward","house of nobles","millstipe","morbent fel","stockade"},rel={"npc:dextren-ward","quest:377","npc:councilman-millstipe","zone:stockade","subzone:darkshire","quest:55","topic:house-of-nobles","zone:duskwood"},src={"Hand of Dextren Ward","Crime and Punishment (Classic)"}}
E["item:head-of-bazil-thredd"] = {t="item",n="Head of Bazil Thredd",z="stockade",s="Warden Thelwater demands proof that the Stockade uprising has been crushed. The severed head of Bazil Thredd is meant to show that the rebellion's leader is dead and Defias control of Stormwind's prison has ended.",h="Warden Thelwater demands proof that the Stockade uprising has been crushed.",sec={{t="Proof of Treason's End",b="Bazil Thredd led the uprising in the Stockade beneath Stormwind City. From his cell block, he directed the riots with the help of loyal Defias inmates. Warden Thelwater distrusts outsiders and struggles to keep order. He demands Thredd's head as proof that the ringleader is dead and to test the adventurer's allegiance to Stormwind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants the Head of Bazil Thredd?",a="Warden Thelwater, at the Stockade entrance, demands Bazil Thredd's head. He wants proof that the ringleader is dead before sharing what he knows about Thredd's conspirators.",al={"who needs thredd head","where to turn in thredd head","thredd head questgiver"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Bazil Thredd?",a="Bazil Thredd was a high-ranking member of the Defias Brotherhood, imprisoned beneath Stormwind. When the prisoners revolted, he took charge and coordinated the uprising from the eastern cell block.",al={"who is bazil thredd","thredd lore","what did bazil do"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Bazil Thredd found?",a="Bazil Thredd is in the eastern wing of the Stockade, at the far end of the block in a central cell. Defias inmates loyal to him guard the cell.",al={"where is thredd","thredd location","how to find bazil thredd"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of Bazil Thredd?",a="It is the severed head of Bazil Thredd, the prisoner orchestrating the rebellion deep within the Stockade. For Warden Thelwater, presenting this grim trophy serves as undeniable physical proof that the ringleader of the prison riot has been permanently eliminated.",al={"what is head of bazil thredd","head of bazil thredd item","bazil thredd head"},it="item",add="4fd859a6"},{q="Where does the Head of Bazil Thredd come from?",a="It is taken directly from Bazil Thredd after you confront and slay him in his cell within Stormwind's Stockade, where he directs the uprising under the protection of his brute guards.",al={"where to get bazil thredd head","how do you get head of bazil thredd","source of bazil thredd head"},it="origin",add="fe91a8a0"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Thredd's severed head calms immediate panic in the capital and proves the crown's justice can reach the rebellious Stockade."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","head of bazil thredd","stockade","the stockade riots","warden thelwater"},rel={"quest:391","zone:stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","quest:389"},src={"Head of Bazil Thredd","The Stockade Riots"}}
E["item:head-of-deepfury"] = {t="item",n="Head of Deepfury",z="stockade",s="At the Stormwind Stockade, Kam Deepfury’s severed head marks the end of a Dark Iron conspirator. His death in the prison riots answers the grievance of the dwarven defenders at Dun Modr.",h="At the Stormwind Stockade, Kam Deepfury’s severed head marks the end of a Dark Iron conspirator.",sec={{t="A Conspirator's Justice",b="Kam Deepfury was held in the Stormwind Stockade for political reasons, spared immediate execution by human diplomacy. Roggo uncovered that Deepfury had orchestrated the attack on the Thandol Span, which cost the lives of King Magni’s soldiers and Longbraid the Grim’s kin. The Ironforge mountaineers at Dun Modr could not accept his continued imprisonment. Bound to his post, Motley Garmason sent Alliance champions into the rioting prison to take Deepfury’s head and deliver dwarven vengeance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury was a Dark Iron dwarf who helped plan the sabotage of the Thandol Span, the land bridge between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. His conspiracy cost dwarven defenders their lives, including Longbraid the Grim’s brother.",al={"kam deepfury lore","who is deepfury","kam deepfury backstory"}},{q="Why was Kam Deepfury in the Stockade instead of executed?",a="Stormwind authorities held Deepfury alive for political reasons. The Ironforge mountaineers saw this restraint as an outrage and demanded his death.",al={"why was deepfury imprisoned","why stockade"}},{q="Who wants the Head of Deepfury?",a="Motley Garmason, stationed at Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands, wants the head. Bound by honor to remain at his post beside Longbraid the Grim, he sends someone to do what he cannot.",al={"who takes deepfury head","fury runs deep turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does bringing back the head accomplish?",a="Bringing Deepfury’s severed head to Dun Modr answers the grievance of the mourning dwarven families. It avenges Longbraid the Grim’s slain brother and shows that human political maneuvering will not bury crimes against Ironforge.",al={"why bring deepfury head","fury runs deep result"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Head of Deepfury?",a="It is the severed head of Kam Deepfury, an incarcerated Dark Iron dwarf held deep within the Stormwind Stockade. You claim it as irrefutable physical proof that the conspirator behind the disastrous assault on the Thandol Span has finally faced justice.",al={"head of deepfury","what is head of deepfury","kam deepfury head"},it="identity",add="42407f6f"},{q="Where does the Head of Deepfury come from?",a="The head is taken directly from Kam Deepfury himself within the cells of the Stockade beneath Stormwind City. Though he was locked away by human authorities rather than executed, you must cut him down in his cell to retrieve it.",al={"where to get head of deepfury","who drops head of deepfury","deepfury head source"},it="origin",add="ff6e9a29"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Ironforge dwarves, taking Deepfury’s head answers the grievance over the Dark Iron treachery at the Thandol Span.",["faction:Alliance"]="The demand for Deepfury’s head reveals friction within the Alliance: Stormwind’s human authorities favor legal caution, while Ironforge’s mountaineers demand harsh justice."},kw={"deepfury","dun modr","head of deepfury","kam deepfury","longbraid","motley garmason","stockade","thandol span"},rel={"quest:378","npc:kam-deepfury","zone:stockade","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Head of Deepfury","The Fury Runs Deep"}}
E["item:head-of-targorr"] = {t="item",n="Head of Targorr",z="stockade",s="In the Stormwind Stockade, Targorr the Dread awaits an execution stopped by nobles in Stormwind. Once Gath'Ilzogg's supreme executioner in the Redridge Mountains, the captured orc is now the subject of Guard Berton's demand for proof of his death in Lakeshire.",h="In the Stormwind Stockade, Targorr the Dread awaits an execution stopped by nobles in Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Delayed Execution",b="Targorr the Dread earned infamy across Redridge as the Blackrock clan warlord Gath'Ilzogg's brutal executioner. He tortured and slaughtered defenders of the Kingdom of Stormwind before his capture and death sentence in the Stormwind Stockade. Stormwind nobles intervened and mysteriously suspended the sentence. Guardsmen like Berton suspect foul play and corruption in the capital.",sp=0},{t="Frontier Justice",b="Guard Berton fears Targorr could become a political pawn or arrange an escape, so he hires an outside champion to enter the volatile prison and finish what the courts delayed. Taking Targorr's head bypasses the stalled legal system and gives closure to grieving families and Lakeshire's besieged defenders, who suffered under the executioner's blades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Targorr the Dread?",a="Targorr the Dread was an infamous orc executioner of the Blackrock clan in Redridge. Under the warlord Gath'Ilzogg, he tortured and executed captured Stormwind soldiers and defenders.",al={"targorr","targorr lore","who is targorr"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Targorr kept alive in the Stockade?",a="Stormwind nobles mysteriously halted Targorr's death sentence through bureaucratic intervention. Lakeshire guards suspect political foul play and corruption, and fear he is being kept as a bargaining chip.",al={"why not execute targorr","targorr stay of execution","stockade trial"},it="history"},{q="Who wants Targorr's head?",a="Guard Berton, stationed outside the Lakeshire Inn, wants Targorr's severed head. After seeing the carnage he caused in the Redridge Mountains, Berton seeks proof that the executioner can never be freed.",al={"who takes targorr head","guard berton","turn in head of targorr"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Targorr found?",a="Targorr the Dread is held in the Stormwind Stockade, behind iron bars in the central cell blocks with rioting inmates.",al={"targorr location","find targorr","where in stockade"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of Targorr?",a="It is the severed head of Targorr the Dread, the notorious supreme Executioner who served under the Blackrock warlord Gath'Ilzogg. Targorr was captured and held in the Stormwind Stockade under sentence of death for torturing and executing brave defenders of the kingdom.",al={"what is head of targorr","head of targorr info","targorr head description"},it="identity",add="1b8c229f",nx={6}},{q="Where does the Head of Targorr come from?",a="The head comes from Targorr the Dread himself, locked away deep inside the Stormwind Stockade. After a Stormwind noble halted his scheduled execution, Guard Berton tasks an adventurer with taking matters into their own hands, slipping into the prison cells to strike off the ruthless orc's head.",al={"where does head of targorr come from","who drops head of targorr","targorr head origin"},it="origin",add="29061798"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions defending Redridge, Targorr's death avenges the slaughtered defenders of Lakeshire and bypasses corrupt noble bureaucracy in Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may share the soldiers' and town guards' grudge against Targorr for torturing captured Kingdom troops during the Blackrock offensive."},kw={"blackrock","gath'ilzogg","guard berton","head of targorr","lakeshire","redridge","stockade","targorr","targorr the dread"},rel={"quest:386","npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:guard-berton","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","subzone:lakeshire","npc:gath-ilzogg","zone:redridge"},src={"Head of Targorr","What Comes Around..."}}
E["item:red-wool-bandana"] = {t="item",n="Red Wool Bandana",z="stockade",s="Inside the Stormwind Stockade, Red Wool Bandana scraps mark Defias brotherhood. Imprisoned cutthroats tear them from jailhouse wool blankets and wear them as emblems of defiance behind bars.",h="Inside the Stormwind Stockade, Red Wool Bandana scraps mark Defias brotherhood.",sec={{t="Stitched in Defiance",b="In the Stormwind Stockade, Defias Brotherhood inmates hold fast to their identity. They secretly tear scraps from prison wool blankets and stitch them into red bandanas to wear as their colors. Guards treat the scarves as contraband, and their discovery can spark fatal mutinies. For the prisoners, each bandana declares that their brotherhood and rebellion endure, even in chains.",sp=0},{t="A Grandmother's Vengeance",b="Red Wool Bandanas became known for the death of Mac Raskol, a fourteen-year-old prison guard. He caught inmates shredding blankets to make the scarves and tried to discipline them. Defias convicts stabbed him in the back. His grieving grandmother, Nikova, now seeks adventurers to enter the rioting dungeon, cull the rioters, and bring back the crimson cloth as proof of vengeance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do prisoners get these bandanas in the Stockade?",a="Defias inmates tear the bandanas from their prison-issue wool blankets. Disarmed and imprisoned, they turn their meager bedding into signs of defiance to wear inside the cells.",al={"where do bandanas come from","stockade bandana source","how do they make red bandanas"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants these bandanas collected?",a="Nikova Raskol, a grieving grandmother in Stormwind, asks adventurers to collect the bandanas. Her fourteen-year-old grandson Mac guarded the Stockade and was murdered by prisoners after he caught them making the scarves.",al={"who needs red wool bandanas","color of blood quest giver","nikova raskol bandana"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the prisoners care so much about wearing red scarves?",a="The Defias Brotherhood uses red masks and bandanas as its gang colors and uniform. Behind bars, the scraps let inmates keep their rank, morale, and unity.",al={"why red bandanas","defias red symbol","meaning of red bandana"},it="purpose"},{q="Which inmates carry them?",a="Almost any rioting Defias member in the Stockade carries one, including Defias Captives, Inmates, Prisoners, Insurgents, and Convicts.",al={"who drops red wool bandana","stockade bandana drops"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is a Red Wool Bandana?",a="A Red Wool Bandana is a makeshift crimson scarf fashioned by imprisoned members of the Defias Brotherhood inside the Stormwind Stockade. By shredding and dying their prison-issued wool blankets, the inmates craft these cloth tokens to openly display their allegiance to the Brotherhood and maintain their gang identity even behind bars.",al={"what is red wool bandana","red wool bandana item","stockade red bandana"},it="identity",add="7f0c1a2a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance defenders, recovering these bandanas brings grim justice for young Mac Raskol and strikes at the rioters holding the city's prison.",["profession:Tailoring"]="These rough bandanas show how desperate hands in captivity can unravel coarse wool blankets and put the fibers to use again."},kw={"defias","mac raskol","nikova raskol","red wool bandana","stormwind","the color of blood","the stockade"},rel={"quest:388","zone:stockade","npc:nikova-raskol","topic:defias-brotherhood","quest:65","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Red Wool Bandana","The Color of Blood"}}
E["npc:bazil-thredd"] = {t="npc",n="Bazil Thredd",z="stockade",s="In the Stormwind Stockade, Bazil Thredd leads the Defias inmates in revolt from the eastern cell block. Edwin VanCleef's lieutenant has been imprisoned there since the Stonemasons' riots.",h="In the Stormwind Stockade, Bazil Thredd leads the Defias inmates in revolt from the eastern cell block.",sec={{t="VanCleef's Lieutenant",b="Bazil Thredd stood beside Edwin VanCleef when the Stonemasons Guild rose against Stormwind's nobility. The guild had been refused payment for rebuilding the city, and VanCleef rejected the government's appeasements and sparked open revolt. Thredd served as his chief lieutenant and most trusted assistant. The city guard captured Thredd during the violent clashes that followed. VanCleef and the surviving masons fled into Westfall and formed the Defias Brotherhood, while Thredd was sent into the Stormwind Stockade.",sp=0},{t="The Stockade Uprising",b="A prison riot has overrun the guards, opened the cells, and turned the Stockade into an armed fortress beneath the Mage Quarter. Thredd commands the imprisoned Defias bandits, insurgents, and allied cutthroats from a post in the eastern wing, guarded by an ogre named Hamhock. For years, he had stayed silent behind bars, seemingly forsaken. Now Warden Thelwater wants Thredd's head, hoping to break the rebellion's leadership before the chaos reaches the city streets.",sp=0},{t="The Curious Visitor",b="A man using the name Maelik began visiting Bazil Thredd once or twice a week a few months before the uprising. Warden Thelwater had long thought the Brotherhood abandoned Thredd to rot, and the visits raised his suspicions. Yet Maelik's papers proved entirely legitimate. Thelwater doubts the visitor will return now that Thredd is dead. Anyone carrying papers that good is well connected, and the visits suggest outside hands in the city had reached the Defias lieutenant.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bazil Thredd?",a="Bazil Thredd was Edwin VanCleef's right hand during the Stonemasons' rebellion in Stormwind. Captured in the riots and imprisoned in the Stockade, he now leads the mutinous inmates.",al={"bazil thredd lore","who is thredd","stockade boss thredd"}},{q="Where can Bazil Thredd be found?",a="Bazil Thredd is deep inside the Stormwind Stockade, beneath the Canal District near the Mage Quarter. From the main hallway intersection, take the eastern cell block and pass the ogre Hamhock; Thredd commands from the center cell in the far chamber.",al={"where is bazil thredd","thredd location","find bazil thredd"}},{q="Why is the Stockade rioting?",a="The inmates have overpowered the guards, opened the cells, and taken the Stockade's halls. Bazil Thredd, the prison's most important Defias prisoner, commands the rioting bandits and convicts while Warden Thelwater tries to keep the revolt from reaching Stormwind's streets.",al={"why are they rioting","stockade riot cause","why did prisoners revolt"}},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater want Thredd dead?",a="Warden Thelwater believes the uprising cannot be quelled while Thredd directs it. With the guards overwhelmed and inmates holding the complex, he orders Thredd executed to break the rebellion's command.",al={"why kill thredd","thelwater bounty thredd","head of bazil thredd reason"}},{q="Who was visiting Thredd before the riot?",a="A quiet man using the name Maelik visited Thredd once or twice a week in the months before the uprising. Thelwater distrusted him, but his papers were legitimate, suggesting well connected hands in the city had reached the Defias lieutenant.",al={"thredd visitor","who is maelik","curious visitor identity"},sp=1},{q="What was Thredd's role in the Stonemasons Guild?",a="Thredd was Edwin VanCleef's principal lieutenant during Stormwind's rebuilding and the labor disputes that followed. He helped lead the guild's resistance after the House of Nobles refused to pay for their work.",al={"was thredd a mason","thredd stonemason","stonemason thredd"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="A Defias revolt beneath Stormwind's streets threatens the capital, and Warden Thelwater wants its leader dealt with before it spreads.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you face a living reminder of the Stonemasons' riots that set the Defias Brotherhood against the kingdom."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","defias brotherhood","edwin vancleef","hamhock","maelik","stockade","stonemasons","stormwind stockade","thredd","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","npc:edwin-vancleef","topic:defias-brotherhood","npc:hamhock","npc:baros-alexston","item:head-of-bazil-thredd"},src={"Bazil Thredd","Bazil Thredd (quest)","The Stockade Riots","The Curious Visitor"}}
E["npc:bruegal-ironknuckle"] = {t="npc",n="Bruegal Ironknuckle",z="stockade",s="Bruegal Ironknuckle prowls the riot-torn halls of the Stormwind Stockade. The dangerous dwarf is a powerful brawler, and anyone trying to restore order may meet his fists.",h="Bruegal Ironknuckle prowls the riot-torn halls of the Stormwind Stockade.",sec={{t="A Dangerous Convict",b="Bruegal Ironknuckle roams the Stormwind Stockade during its open revolt. The dangerous dwarf is known for his brutal brawling strength. Many of the city's most volatile cutthroats have seized the underground cellblocks, and Bruegal is among them. He does not stay in one cell, but prowls the riot-torn halls, ready to bash anyone trying to quell the uprising.",sp=0},{t="Unruly Outlaw",b="Bruegal Ironknuckle is one of many rogues and outlaws held deep beneath Stormwind. The Defias Brotherhood and its ringleaders direct much of the revolt, while inmates like Bruegal show that the prison holds criminals from across the eastern realms. Whatever crimes brought him there, his fierce resilience makes him elusive and one of the deadliest lone inmates in the corridors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bruegal Ironknuckle?",a="Bruegal Ironknuckle is an elite dwarven convict in the Stormwind Stockade. During the ongoing riot, he wanders the prison halls and is difficult to find.",al={"who is bruegal","ironknuckle lore","stockade dwarf prisoner"},it="identity"},{q="Is Bruegal Ironknuckle part of the Defias Brotherhood?",a="Bruegal is a dwarven prisoner in the Stockade. His precise affiliation is not recorded.",al={"is bruegal defias","defias dwarf stockade"},it="side"},{q="Why is he imprisoned in the Stockade?",a="The charges that brought Bruegal to the Stockade are not recorded in public warrants. His violent temper and brawling reputation suggest serious offenses against Stormwind's laws.",al={"why is bruegal locked up","bruegal crime"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can he be found inside the Stockade?",a="Bruegal roams the Stockade's inner passages and junctions instead of staying in one cell. He may surprise those clearing the rioters.",al={"bruegal spawn","where is bruegal","stockade rare spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is he always present in the prison?",a="No. Bruegal appears only sporadically during the unrest. He is often locked down or hidden from sight.",al={"can bruegal not spawn","why cant i find bruegal"},gp=true},{q="What makes him notable among the prisoners?",a="Bruegal is known for his fearsome fighting skill. He is also reputed to hide valuable contraband and gear from the guards, making him a sought-after prize for those brave enough to face him.",al={"why do people look for bruegal","bruegal significance"},it="fame"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may find it sobering to see a stout kinsman among Stormwind's cutpurses and rogues. Exile and outlawry reach even the sons of Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can help Stormwind's city guard suppress rogues like Ironknuckle, who threaten to turn the capital's heart into a fortress of anarchy.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can see in Ironknuckle's raw grit and heavy fists the brute strength that remains when discipline and honor fall away."},kw={"brawler","bruegal ironknuckle","dwarf","inmate","ironknuckle","prisoner","rare","stockade","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:dwarf"},src={"Bruegal Ironknuckle"}}
E["npc:councilman-millstipe"] = {t="npc",n="Councilman Millstipe",z="stockade",s="Darkshire's council grows bitter as Stormwind overrides its judgment. Councilman Millstipe lives in the town hall and wants justice for Duskwood's people.",h="Darkshire's council grows bitter as Stormwind overrides its judgment.",sec={{t="Justice Denied by Stormwind",b="Darkshire faces undead and attacks from ferocious beasts, while its council struggles against Stormwind City's bureaucracy. Councilman Millstipe reflects the town's growing bitterness toward the crown. The notorious grave robber Dextren Ward was caught selling freshly dug corpses to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Darkshire's leaders sentenced Ward to death, but Stormwind's House of Nobles commuted the execution and locked him away in the Stormwind Stockade.",sp=0},{t="A Message to the Nobles",b="Councilman Millstipe believes Stormwind's politicians have put Duskwood's safety and justice aside. He discreetly directs adventurers to kill Dextren Ward in his Stockade cell. The order defies the House of Nobles and warns that, if Stormwind will not protect Duskwood's people, they will take justice into their own hands.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Councilman Millstipe be found?",a="Councilman Millstipe can be found inside Darkshire's town hall, in eastern Duskwood.",al={"millstipe location","where is millstipe","find councilman millstipe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Millstipe want Dextren Ward dead?",a="Dextren Ward was a grave robber who dug up Duskwood's dead and sold them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Lord Ebonlocke sentenced him to be beheaded, but Stormwind's House of Nobles spared him and sent him to the Stockade.",al={"why kill dextren ward","millstipe dextren ward","ward crime"},it="target"},{q="What is Millstipe's grievance with Stormwind?",a="Millstipe believes Stormwind has abandoned Duskwood while interfering with its local justice. The House of Nobles overturned Darkshire's death sentence for Dextren Ward, leaving the settlement feeling ignored and unprotected by the throne.",al={"why mad at stormwind","house of nobles darkshire","millstipe politics"},it="conflict"},{q="Does Millstipe have any known family?",a="No family of Councilman Millstipe is known.",al={"millstipe relatives","dorothea millstipe","millstipe family"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Councilman Millstipe?",a="Councilman Millstipe is a prominent member of the council governing Darkshire in Duskwood. Frustrated by Stormwind's neglect and bureaucratic meddling, he works within the town hall to protect his beleaguered people, fiercely defying distant nobles who undermine Duskwood's frontier justice.",al={"who is millstipe","councilman millstipe","who is councilman millstipe"},it="identity",add="2e4c6610"},{q="Whose side is Councilman Millstipe on?",a="Millstipe is loyal to the people of Darkshire and the Council of Duskwood. Though formally part of the Grand Alliance, he harbors bitter resentment toward the corrupt House of Nobles in Stormwind, standing firmly for his local township against distant bureaucrats who refuse to send aid.",al={"millstipe faction","is millstipe alliance","who does millstipe serve"},it="side",add="926d4bb5"},{q="What does Councilman Millstipe want?",a="Millstipe seeks frontier justice for Duskwood and wants to send an unmistakable message to the House of Nobles. Disgusted that nobles spared the grave robber Dextren Ward from execution, Millstipe demands Ward's death within the Stockade to prove Duskwood will not tolerate Stormwind's corrupt interference.",al={"millstipe goal","what does millstipe want","councilman millstipe goal"},it="wants",add="78c3778b"},{q="Why is Councilman Millstipe here?",a="Millstipe remains in Darkshire's town hall to fulfill his civic duties on the council. From there, he navigates Duskwood's worsening perils, coordinating local administration and enlisting independent champions to enact the sentences that Stormwind's magistrates refuse to carry out.",al={"why is millstipe in duskwood","millstipe location why","what is millstipe doing in darkshire"},it="why_here",add="7f6b4a90"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Millstipe shows the political divide between Stormwind's sheltered nobility and Duskwood's desperate frontier settlements, which receive little aid and face heavy-handed interference from the capital.",["class:Rogue"]="For a rogue willing to enter the heavily guarded Stockade and carry out an unsanctioned political execution, Millstipe offers work that defies the House of Nobles."},kw={"councilman millstipe","darkshire","dextren ward","duskwood","house of nobles","millstipe","morbent fel","stockade"},rel={"quest:377","npc:dextren-ward","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","subzone:stormwind-stockade","quest:55","topic:house-of-nobles"},src={"Councilman Millstipe"}}
E["npc:dextren-ward"] = {t="npc",n="Dextren Ward",z="stockade",s="In the Stormwind Stockade, Dextren Ward remains a prisoner amid a bloody uprising. Before his capture, he dug up bodies at Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood and sold them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Darkshire's town council has marked him for death.",h="In the Stormwind Stockade, Dextren Ward remains a prisoner amid a bloody uprising.",sec={{t="Grave Robbery in Duskwood",b="Before chains bound him beneath Stormwind, Dextren Ward robbed graves in Duskwood for profit. At Raven Hill Cemetery, where sorrow and horror had grown, he dug up the newly buried dead. He sold the bodies to local practitioners of dark arts.",sp=0},{t="Pawn of the Necromancer",b="Morbent Fel, a necromancer whose rituals plagued Duskwood and swelled the undead ranks, was Ward's main customer. By supplying him with bodies, Ward helped spread terror through Darkshire. Stormwind authorities eventually captured Ward and brought him to the Stockade. His crimes left the people of Duskwood demanding justice, and Councilman Millstipe called for Ward's hand as proof.",sp=0},{t="Chaos in the Stockade",b="A rebellion swept through the Stockade, and Ward was freed from his cell amid the chaos. Armed and vicious, he seized control of his corner of the prison and uses fear to keep intruders away. Alliance forces seeking to restore order count him among their priority targets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dextren Ward?",a="Dextren Ward is a notorious criminal held in the Stormwind Stockade. In Duskwood, he robbed graves to supply bodies for dark rituals.",al={"who is dextren ward","dextren ward lore","stockade dextren"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Dextren Ward in the Stockade?",a="Stormwind authorities captured Ward for robbing graves at Raven Hill Cemetery in Duskwood. He dug up newly buried bodies and sold them to the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"why was he arrested","dextren ward crime","what did dextren do"},it="why_here"},{q="Who wants Dextren Ward dead?",a="Councilman Millstipe of Darkshire wants Ward dead. He demands Ward's hand as proof of justice for the desecrated graves of Duskwood.",al={"who wants dextren dead","dextren ward bounty","crime and punishment questgiver"},it="target"},{q="What is Ward's connection to Morbent Fel?",a="Ward supplied corpses to Morbent Fel. He dug up the newly buried dead at Raven Hill Cemetery for the necromancer's dark rituals.",al={"morbent fel connection","dextren ward morbent fel","who bought the bodies"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Dextren Ward be found?",a="Dextren Ward is inside the Stormwind Stockade, the prison in Stormwind City's canals. During the ongoing revolt, he is in one of its holding wings.",al={"dextren ward location","where is dextren ward","where to find dextren"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the quest require Dextren's hand?",a="Councilman Millstipe asks for Ward's dead hand as proof that the grave robber can no longer dig up Duskwood's graves or profit from necromancy.",al={"why sever his hand","dextren ward hand","proof of death dextren"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Dextren Ward on?",a="Ward looks out strictly for himself, though he had dealings with the dark forces plaguing Duskwood. Rather than fighting for an organized faction like the Defias Brotherhood, he operated as a criminal opportunist, striking a foul partnership to supply freshly dug corpses from Raven Hill Cemetery to the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"dextren ward faction","who does dextren ward work for","is dextren ward defias"},it="side",add="87b921a6"},{q="Why is Dextren Ward feared?",a="Beyond his gruesome trade as a grave robber, Ward is known to strike panic into the hearts of any who face him. In the cramped, violent halls of the Stockade, his ability to sow supernatural terror makes him exceptionally lethal, as a fleeing fighter quickly runs right into the blades of other rioting inmates.",al={"why is dextren ward dangerous","dextren ward feared","what makes dextren ward dangerous"},it="fame",add="371c7358"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion helping Darkshire, ending Ward's crimes brings justice for Duskwood's desecrated graves and helps reclaim the rioting Stockade.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see Ward's work with necromancers and fresh corpses as an offense against the Light and the peaceful rest of the dead.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see Ward's desecration of Raven Hill's burial ground as a matter of moral and spiritual restitution."},kw={"councilman millstipe","crime and punishment","dextren ward","duskwood","grave robber","morbent fel","raven hill cemetery","stormwind","the stockade"},rel={"quest:377","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","npc:councilman-millstipe","subzone:raven-hill-cemetery","quest:55","quest:163","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Dextren Ward"}}
E["npc:hamhock"] = {t="npc",n="Hamhock",z="stockade",s="In the Stormwind Stockade, Hamhock remains locked among the rioting prisoners. The massive two-headed ogre is one of the prison’s most brutal inmates.",h="In the Stormwind Stockade, Hamhock remains locked among the rioting prisoners.",sec={{t="A Brute Behind Bars",b="Hamhock is a towering two-headed ogre in the Stormwind Stockade. The prison was built for petty thieves, murderers, and political dissidents, so his size makes him an imposing presence among the cells. When the prisoners rose up and took control, Hamhock stayed amid the disorder, crushing anyone who entered his cellblock.",sp=0},{t="Murky Origins",b="No record tells how Hamhock was captured or why he was locked among Stormwind’s thieves and dissidents. Whatever brought him to the Stockade, he is now one of its most dangerous inmates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hamhock?",a="Hamhock is a massive two-headed ogre held in the Stormwind Stockade. During the uprising led by Defias convicts, he is a danger deep in the prison corridors.",al={"hamhock","who is the ogre in stockade","ogre boss stockade"},it="identity"},{q="How did an ogre end up in the Stormwind Stockade?",a="No record tells how Hamhock was captured or brought to Stormwind.",al={"why is hamhock in jail","how did hamhock get captured","why is there an ogre in stockades"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Hamhock allied with the Defias rioters?",a="The Defias ringleaders lead the prison rebellion, but no one knows whether Hamhock works with them or simply revels in the chaos among the broken cells.",al={"is hamhock defias","hamhock defias brotherhood","does hamhock work for bazil"},it="side"},{q="Is Hamhock related to the ogres in Duskwood?",a="Nothing ties Hamhock to the ogres in Duskwood. The Splinter Fist ogres at Duskwood’s Vul'Gol Ogre Mound are the nearest ogre clan to Stormwind, but no record tells where Hamhock came from.",al={"is hamhock splinter fist","hamhock vulgol","vul'gol ogres stockade"},it="ties"},{q="Is Hamhock tied to any specific bounty or quest?",a="No bounty or city warrant names Hamhock. He is a danger encountered while adventurers clear the rioting stronghold.",al={"hamhock quest","is there a quest for hamhock","hamhock bounty"},gp=true},{q="Why are two-headed ogres significant?",a="Two-headed ogres have distinct personalities in each head and are often more cunning or magically adept than their single-headed kin. That makes Hamhock exceptionally dangerous to ordinary prison guards.",al={"two headed ogre lore","why two heads"},it="origin"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="An unrestrained two-headed ogre beneath the capital’s streets shows how completely the city guards have lost control of the Stockade.",["class:Warrior"]="To subdue Hamhock, a warrior must meet his hulking strength head-on in the prison’s narrow halls."},kw={"duskwood","hamhock","ogre","prison","splinter fist","stockade","stormwind","two-headed"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:defias-brotherhood","subzone:vul-gol-ogre-mound","zone:duskwood","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Hamhock"}}
E["npc:kam-deepfury"] = {t="npc",n="Kam Deepfury",z="stockade",s="In Stormwind's Stockade, Kam Deepfury waits apart from the Defias rebels. The Dark Iron dwarf was captured after arranging the blast that shattered the Thandol Span, far to the north.",h="In Stormwind's Stockade, Kam Deepfury waits apart from the Defias rebels.",sec={{t="A Saboteur Far from Home",b="Kam Deepfury is a Dark Iron dwarf held deep in the Stormwind Stockade. Most prisoners there are disgruntled Stonemasons or Defias rebels, but he belongs to neither. Captured and brought to Stormwind after an operation crippled vital northern infrastructure, he remains cut off from his kin beneath Blackrock Mountain. Like the rebels who share the corridors, he is hostile to the Alliance.",sp=0},{t="The Thandol Span Sabotage",b="Alliance intelligence at Dun Modr, near the Wetlands' northern border, named Kam Deepfury as the chief architect of the blast that shattered the Thandol Span. The explosion severed one of the massive stone bridges linking the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. It crippled a vital trade and military route for Ironforge and the Alliance, and killed a kin of the dwarf commander Longbraid the Grim.",sp=0},{t="A Score to Settle",b="Motley Garmason and the grieving Longbraid the Grim seek mercenaries in the Wetlands to reach Kam Deepfury in Stormwind's riot-torn Stockade. The Dark Iron insurrectionist has found brief shelter from his victims' relatives in prison. Those seeking him want his head, to settle a bloody grudge begun hundreds of miles to the north.",sp=1,bt={"q303.3"}}},faq={{q="Who is Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury is a Dark Iron dwarf prisoner held in the Stormwind Stockade. He is known for arranging the sabotage of the Thandol Span and has no allegiance to the Defias rebels imprisoned beside him.",al={"who is deepfury","kam deepfury lore","who is the dwarf in stockades"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a Dark Iron dwarf locked in the Stormwind Stockade?",a="Kam Deepfury was captured after coordinating the blast that shattered one of the Thandol Span's bridges. The explosion killed a dwarf kin of Longbraid the Grim and cut a vital crossing between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands.",al={"why is he in stockade","what did kam deepfury do","why is he imprisoned"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Kam Deepfury part of the Defias Brotherhood?",a="No. Kam Deepfury is a Dark Iron dwarf, not a member of the Defias Brotherhood. He is imprisoned alongside the rebels but shares their hostility toward the Alliance.",al={"is he defias","kam deepfury defias","is deepfury working with vancleef"},it="side"},{q="Who wants Kam Deepfury dead?",a="Motley Garmason and Longbraid the Grim seek Kam Deepfury's death. The bombing of the Thandol Span killed a kin of Longbraid the Grim, and the two seek mercenaries to reach Deepfury in Stormwind's Stockade.",al={"who gave the quest for deepfury","who wants deepfury killed"}},{q="Where did Kam Deepfury commit his crime?",a="Kam Deepfury organized the sabotage at the Thandol Span, where a bridge links the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where was the bridge blown up","deepfury bridge bombing","thandol span attack"},it="history"},{q="Where can Kam Deepfury be found inside the Stockade?",a="Kam Deepfury is held deep within the cell blocks of the Stormwind Stockade, beneath Stormwind's canal district.",al={"where is deepfury in stockade","kam deepfury location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Kam Deepfury allied with?",a="Kam Deepfury belongs to the hostile Dark Iron dwarf clan. Although he is held alongside rebellious cutpurses and convicts in the Stormwind Stockade, he has no ties to the Defias Brotherhood. His allegiance lies entirely with his own shadowy clan, operating far north of his homeland to strike deep into Alliance-held territory.",al={"kam deepfury ties","who does kam deepfury work for","kam deepfury faction"},it="ties",add="1bde1b20"},{q="Why is Kam Deepfury infamous?",a="Kam Deepfury earned his grim notoriety by masterminding the catastrophic explosion that shattered one of the massive stone bridges across the Thandol Span. The violent sabotage not only compromised a critical artery between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands, but it also claimed the life of a dwarven kin of Longbraid the Grim.",al={"kam deepfury reputation","why is kam deepfury feared","what did kam deepfury do"},it="fame",add="45416a5d"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you know Kam Deepfury as the saboteur who shattered the Thandol Span and killed a kin of Longbraid the Grim. Avenge that loss in the name of honor.",["faction:Alliance"]="While Stormwind focuses on the Defias uprising, Kam Deepfury reminds the Alliance of the Dark Iron threat to its northern frontiers."},kw={"dark iron","deepfury","dun modr","garmason","kam deepfury","longbraid","stockade","stormwind","thandol span"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-modr","quest:378","npc:longbraid-the-grim","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:defias-brotherhood","topic:alliance"},src={"Kam Deepfury"}}
E["npc:targorr-the-dread"] = {t="npc",n="Targorr the Dread",z="stockade",s="Deep in the Stormwind Stockade, Targorr the Dread waits among the rioting convicts. His execution was delayed by corruption and neglect, and the Defias uprising gave him a chance to escape.",h="Deep in the Stormwind Stockade, Targorr the Dread waits among the rioting convicts.",sec={{t="The Butcher of Redridge",b="Before his capture, Targorr the Dread served Warlord Gath'Ilzogg as the Blackrock clan's supreme executioner. He worked from the occupied ruins in Redridge, where his cruelty surpassed even the Dark Horde's violent ways. Stormwind guards and militiamen who defended the borderlands suffered torment and slow deaths at his hands. Across the kingdom, few names were more reviled.",sp=0},{t="Justice Denied",b="After Alliance forces captured Targorr alive, they brought him in chains to the capital and locked him in the high-security Stockade. His execution stalled in Stormwind's judicial and political bureaucracy. Graft, endless paperwork, and neglect kept the courts from delivering the death sentence he had earned. A bloodthirsty war criminal remained in a cell beneath the heart of the city.",sp=0},{t="Uprising in the Cells",b="When the Defias Brotherhood broke prisoners out by force, Targorr seized his chance. He escaped his cell and joined the Defias rioters, turning his cellblock into a slaughterhouse. Warden Thelwater has lost control of the prison. Lakeshire still bears the wounds Targorr dealt its defenders, and seeks adventurers willing to enter the riots and bring back the butcher's head.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Targorr the Dread?",a="Targorr the Dread served Warlord Gath'Ilzogg as a Blackrock orc and supreme executioner. He became notorious for torturing captured Stormwind soldiers, until he was caught and imprisoned in the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"who is targorr","targorr lore","stockade orc boss"},it="identity"},{q="Why wasn't Targorr executed when he was captured?",a="Stormwind's inefficient, bloated, and corrupt legal administration delayed Targorr's execution with endless paperwork. The prison riots erupted before the courts could carry out his sentence.",al={"why wasn't he killed","why is targorr alive","stormwind corruption"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is an orc allied with the Defias Brotherhood?",a="During the prison uprising, convicts of all stripes united against their jailers. Targorr joined the Defias rioters to secure his freedom and slaughter any guards or adventurers who cross his path.",al={"why defias working with orcs","targorr defias ally","stockade orcs"},it="side"},{q="Who wants Targorr dead now?",a="Guard Berton, stationed in Lakeshire in Redridge, offers a bounty for Targorr's severed head. Lakeshire suffered under Targorr's cruelty and wants the execution Stormwind's courts failed to deliver.",al={"who gives the targorr quest","guard berton targorr","targorr bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Targorr be found?",a="Targorr is inside the Stormwind Stockade, in a rear cellblock with other rioting inmates.",al={"where is targorr","targorr location","stockade room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What clan does Targorr belong to?",a="Targorr belongs to the Blackrock orcs, among the rogue Dark Horde remnants operating from the Redridge Mountains and Blackrock Spire. They are not part of the New Horde led by Thrall.",al={"targorr clan","is targorr horde","blackrock targorr"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Targorr the Dread so feared?",a="Targorr earned his terrifying reputation as the supreme executioner for the Blackrock orcs under General Gath'Ilzogg. His cruelty was notorious even by the brutal standards of his clan. Rather than granting honorable deaths to fallen foes, he subjected captured defenders of Stormwind to ruthless torture on a whim, cementing his infamy among the people of Redridge and the kingdom at large.",al={"why is targorr feared","targorr the dread reputation","why is targorr famous"},it="fame",add="eed5e381"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, especially those with ties to Redridge, Targorr recalls the cost of the kingdom's bureaucratic failures and the ongoing threat of the Blackrock orcs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Putting down Targorr amid the Stockade riots brings long-overdue justice to Lakeshire's fallen defenders and helps contain the chaos beneath the capital."},kw={"berton","blackrock","dread","executioner","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","stockade","targorr"},rel={"zone:stockade","quest:386","npc:guard-berton","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stormwind-stockade","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Targorr the Dread"}}
E["npc:warden-thelwater"] = {t="npc",n="Warden Thelwater",z="stockade",s="In Stormwind, a prison riot has left Warden Thelwater besieged at the Stockade entrance. He calls for capable adventurers to stop the Defias prisoners before the uprising reaches the city above.",h="In Stormwind, a prison riot has left Warden Thelwater besieged at the Stockade entrance.",sec={{t="A Crisis in the Canals",b="Beneath Stormwind's canals, the Stockade holds the kingdom's most dangerous miscreants, petty thieves, and political conspirators. Warden Thelwater was charged with keeping them locked away, but an organized revolt caught the guards off guard. The prisoners overwhelmed security and seized the cells, leaving Thelwater barricaded at the entrance as he struggles to contain an armed uprising beneath the capital's streets.",sp=0},{t="Containing the Truth",b="Thelwater wants to keep panic from reaching Stormwind's streets, so he handles the uprising in secret. Bazil Thredd, the revolt's mastermind, holds great influence among the Defias Brotherhood prisoners. Fearing the riot will expose weaknesses in Stormwind's rule, Thelwater turns to outside mercenaries to enter the cellblocks, defeat the ringleaders, and quietly take back the prison.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Warden Thelwater?",a="Warden Thelwater is the human official at the Stockade entrance in Stormwind City. He manages the high-security prison.",al={"thelwater","stockade warden","who is thelwater"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to the Stockade?",a="A coordinated revolt broke out among the prisoners, led chiefly by members of the Defias Brotherhood. They overpowered the guards and seized the cellblocks, leaving Thelwater and his remaining men pinned near the entrance.",al={"stockade riot","what happened in stockades","why is stockades broken"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is leading the prison riot?",a="Bazil Thredd directs the revolt from deep inside the prison. He commands the Defias inmates and led their sudden strike against the guards.",al={"stockade leader","who leads the uprising","who is bazil thredd"},it="threat"},{q="Why hasn't the Stormwind City Guard intervened in force?",a="Thelwater wants to settle the crisis quietly. News that Stormwind's most fortified dungeon fell to its own inmates could spread panic, so he calls on discreet adventurers to regain control inside.",al={"why no guards","why hire adventurers","secret riot"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of prisoners are kept here?",a="The Stockade holds petty crooks, thieves, murderers, and dangerous political insurgents, including high-ranking members of the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"stockade prisoners","who is in stockade","types of criminals"},it="residents"},{q="Where can Warden Thelwater be found?",a="Warden Thelwater is stationed just outside the Stockade entrance, near the canals between the Mage Quarter and Cathedral Square in Stormwind City.",al={"thelwater location","where is warden","find thelwater"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Warden Thelwater on?",a="Thelwater serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and answers to its ruling authority. As the official warden of the Stockade, he represents the city's penal administration and the crown, striving to maintain order beneath the streets and prevent the realm's worst criminals from spilling out into the capital.",al={"thelwater faction","who does thelwater serve","is thelwater alliance"},it="side",add="088280c3"},{q="What does Warden Thelwater want?",a="Thelwater wants the prison uprising ruthlessly suppressed before the chaos spreads. Caught off guard when the Defias rioted, his primary objective is eliminating Bazil Thredd, the mastermind behind the outbreak, and putting down rebel leaders to restore total control over the facility as quietly as possible.",al={"what does thelwater need","thelwater goal","why does thelwater need adventurers"},it="wants",add="bf0ea06f"},{q="Why is Warden Thelwater here?",a="Thelwater is stationed at the entrance of the Stockade because he was forced back when the inmates revolted. Unable to quell the riot alone with his remaining guards, he remains near the canal threshold to hold the line and enlist capable mercenaries to plunge inside and reclaim the cells.",al={"why is thelwater at the stockade","thelwater standing outside","why is thelwater by the entrance"},it="why_here",add="4dddd3c5"},{q="Who is Warden Thelwater tied to?",a="Thelwater is bound to the Stormwind administration and works alongside the city guards tasked with securing the capital. His most pressing connection within the dungeon is his adversarial tie to the prisoner Bazil Thredd, whose coordinated uprising threatens Thelwater's position and the kingdom's security.",al={"thelwater allies","who does thelwater work for","thelwater connections"},it="ties",add="479dc467"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can help Warden Thelwater restore order in Stormwind and keep the prison mutiny from threatening the capital's citizens.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin devoted to order and justice, you can help Warden Thelwater contain violent criminals and restore discipline.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you enter the Stockade amid the fallout of Defias intrigue and prison politics."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","prison","riot","stockade","stormwind","thelwater","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","quest:391","quest:389","quest:387","quest:392","zone:stormwind","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Warden Thelwater"}}
E["quest:377"] = {t="quest",n="Crime and Punishment",z="stockade",s="Crime and Punishment is an Alliance bounty originating in Darkshire that demands the extrajudicial execution of a grave robber imprisoned within the Stormwind Stockade. Councilman Millstipe issues the contract after the House of Nobles overrides Duskwood's death sentence for Dextren Ward. Carrying out the hit satisfies local vengeance while delivering a sharp warning to the capital's negligent aristocracy.",h="Crime and Punishment is an Alliance bounty originating in Darkshire that demands the extrajudicial execution...",sec={{t="Justice Denied in Duskwood",b="Duskwood already suffers beneath a shroud of creeping horrors and official indifference from the capital. When Dextren Ward was caught digging up fresh corpses from the Darkshire cemetery to sell to the necromancer Morbent Fel, the town's ruling council showed no mercy. Lord Ello Ebonlocke sentenced the grave robber to beheadment. However, before the axe could fall, the House of Nobles intervened, claiming Ward as an imperial prisoner and transferring him to the high-security cells of the Stormwind Stockade.",sp=0},{t="An Insult to the Dead",b="To Councilman Millstipe and the grieving citizens of Darkshire, sparing Ward from the headsman's block was an intolerable insult. The nobles in their secure city showed complete disregard for the torment suffered by frontier families whose dead relatives were fed into Fel's dark craft. Frustrated by Stormwind's bureaucratic meddling, Millstipe recruits daring mercenaries to infiltrate the riotous Stockade, assassinate Ward in his cell, and sever his hand as proof of execution.",sp=0},{t="A Message to the Crown",b="Killing Ward is as much a political act as it is closure for the wronged. By ordering the assassination of a high-value prisoner under the crown's own lock and key, the Darkshire Council sends a defiant message back to Stormwind. If the nobility refuses to defend Duskwood or honor its local laws, the town has shown it will enforce its own brand of frontier justice right beneath the regent's nose.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Councilman Millstipe want Dextren Ward dead?",a="Ward was caught robbing the Darkshire cemetery, selling freshly buried corpses to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Lord Ebonlocke sentenced him to beheading, but Stormwind's House of Nobles snatched him away to lock him in the Stockade instead.",al={"why kill dextren ward","what did dextren ward do","millstipe motivation"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Dextren Ward located?",a="He is held deep inside the Stormwind Stockade dungeon in the capital city of Stormwind, located along the far left corridor of the prison complex.",al={"dextren ward location","where is ward","how to find dextren ward"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why didn't Stormwind just execute Dextren Ward?",a="The House of Nobles claimed jurisdiction over Ward for their own unspecified reasons, overruling Darkshire's local sentence and sparking outrage among Duskwood residents who feel abandoned by the capital.",al={"why was ward imprisoned","why stockade not execution"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Millstipe demand Ward's hand?",a="Councilman Millstipe requires indisputable physical proof that the sentence was carried out in defiance of the House of Nobles, offering closure to the victimized families in Duskwood.",al={"hand of dextren ward","why hand proof"},it="item"},{q="Who is Morbent Fel?",a="Morbent Fel is a powerful necromancer haunting Duskwood, animating the dead and orchestrating dark rituals using bodies supplied by unscrupulous scum like Dextren Ward.",al={"who is fel","morbent fel lore"},it="identity"},{q="What does this quest reveal about Duskwood's relationship with Stormwind?",a="It highlights deep political resentment. Duskwood feels neglected and unprotected by the throne, and the council's willingness to send assassins into the capital's prison shows how strained that loyalty has become.",al={"darkshire and stormwind politics","duskwood resentment"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Dextren Ward and why is he in the Stockade?",a="Dextren Ward is a grave robber who dug up corpses from the cemetery in Duskwood and sold them to the necromancer Morbent Fel. Though Lord Ebonlocke sentenced him to death for desecrating the dead, the House of Nobles intervened and hauled him to Stormwind instead, locking him inside the Stockade.",al={"who is dextren ward","why is dextren ward in prison","dextren ward crime"},it="target",add="9b93eafe"},{q="Why does Millstipe need you to kill Ward instead of using local authorities?",a="Ward is locked away deep inside the capital's prison under Stormwind's official jurisdiction. Darkshire's Night Watch has its hands full defending the town from encroaching horrors, and local officials cannot openly send troops to storm a royal dungeon without inciting treason. They need an independent agent to deliver their brand of justice quietly.",al={"why can't darkshire guards kill ward","why hire an adventurer to assassinate ward","why does darkshire need me"},it="why_me",add="444df616"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The quest exposes severe friction within the Alliance heartland, pitting the struggling, neglected frontier of Darkshire against the distant, arrogant bureaucrats of the House of Nobles.",["class:Rogue"]="Millstipe's task is a brazen political assassination requiring a covert infiltration into the crown's own maximum-security penitentiary to bypass royal decree.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the southern kingdoms, this contract tests whether your loyalty lies with the distant crown in Stormwind or the desperate settlers holding the line in Duskwood."},kw={"darkshire","dextren ward","duskwood","grave robber","house of nobles","millstipe","morbent fel","stockade"},rel={"npc:dextren-ward","npc:councilman-millstipe","zone:stockade","zone:duskwood","quest:55","topic:house-of-nobles","subzone:darkshire","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Councilman Millstipe",["end"]="Councilman Millstipe",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=377,ri={"Hand of Dextren Ward"}},src={"Crime and Punishment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:378"] = {t="quest",n="The Fury Runs Deep",z="stockade",s="Motley Garmason seeks vengeance against Kam Deepfury, now held in Stormwind's Stockade. Deepfury planned the assault on the Thandol Span, where Bronzebeard defenders died, including Longbraid the Grim's brother. Stormwind keeps Deepfury as a political prisoner, so Motley turns to an adventurer to carry out dwarven justice.",h="Motley Garmason seeks vengeance against Kam Deepfury, now held in Stormwind's Stockade.",sec={{t="A Grudge Across Continents",b="Clashes between Bronzebeard defenders at Dun Modr and Dark Iron insurgents keep the northern Wetlands in turmoil. When the Thandol Span came under attack, sabotage took the lives of several dwarves, including Longbraid the Grim's brother. Roggo gathered intelligence showing that Kam Deepfury planned the strike. Rather than face execution on the front lines, Deepfury was taken to the Stormwind Stockade as a political prisoner, not executed for murder.",sp=0},{t="Dwarven Retribution vs. Human Law",b="Motley Garmason is stationed at Dun Modr and refuses to let Stormwind's political calculations shield a war criminal. To him, human law puts decorum before blood debts. Bound to remain beside Longbraid in the Wetlands, Motley sends trusted champions beneath the human capital, into the rioting Stockade, to take Deepfury's head and settle the clan's score.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury is a Dark Iron dwarf who planned the attack on the Thandol Span. His plan led to the deaths of Ironforge dwarves guarding the crossing, and survivors in Dun Modr mark him as a target.",al={"deepfury","kam deepfury lore","who is deepfury"},it="target"},{q="Why is Kam Deepfury imprisoned in Stormwind instead of Ironforge?",a="Stormwind authorities captured Kam Deepfury and hold him in the Stockade for political reasons they have not disclosed. The dwarves of Dun Modr see this as bureaucracy that denies them immediate justice.",al={"why is deepfury in stockade","why stockade prisoner"},it="why_here"},{q="Why doesn't Motley Garmason hunt Deepfury down himself?",a="Motley Garmason is stationed at Dun Modr beside Longbraid the Grim, where they face ongoing Dark Iron advances in the northern Wetlands. His honor and military duty keep him from leaving the defensive line for Stormwind.",al={"why motley stay","why motley doesn't go"},it="why_me"},{q="What happened at the Thandol Span?",a="The Dark Iron clan attacked the bridge at the Thandol Span, which connects the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands. The assault killed several Bronzebeard defenders, including Longbraid's brother.",al={"thandol span attack","what happened thandol span"},it="history"},{q="Who uncovered Deepfury's role in the Thandol Span attack?",a="A dwarf named Roggo uncovered intelligence linking Kam Deepfury to the planning and execution of the Thandol Span attack. Roggo gave Motley the proof he needed to demand retribution.",al={"who found deepfury","roggo intelligence"},it="origin"},{q="Is Stormwind's leadership aware of the assassination inside their prison?",a="Motley's order is an unsanctioned dwarven vendetta. He bypasses human law, believing King Magni's soldiers have the right to execute the saboteur while the Stockade is in the grip of riots.",al={"stormwind know about hit","is deepfury kill sanctioned"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Motley Garmason want Kam Deepfury killed?",a="Motley Garmason seeks vengeance for the Dark Iron assault on the Thandol Span, which claimed the lives of King Magni's subjects and Commander Longbraid's brother. Although Kam Deepfury was captured and imprisoned in the Stockade, Motley refuses to allow human diplomacy and bureaucracy to shelter the conspirator from dwarven justice. He wants Deepfury executed so the fallen can finally be avenged and their kin can find closure.",al={"why kill deepfury","motley garmason motive","why does motley want deepfury dead"},it="motive",add="323f2e11"},{q="What is the Head of Deepfury for?",a="Motley Garmason demands the severed head of Kam Deepfury as irrefutable proof that the treacherous Dark Iron conspirator has truly met his end. Knowing that Stormwind's guards merely intend to hold Deepfury for political leverage, Motley will not rest until he sees physical evidence that justice has been delivered for Longbraid's family and the defenders of Dun Modr.",al={"why take deepfury head","head of deepfury purpose","what is deepfury head used for"},it="item",add="e14999ea"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves, killing Deepfury settles a blood debt and honors the clanmates who died defending the Thandol Span.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you face your kingdom's diplomatic choices when you set aside Stormwind's prison policies to meet your dwarven allies' code of justice.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you see the strain between Stormwind's legal pragmatism and Ironforge's demand for direct vengeance in wartime."},kw={"dark iron war","deepfury","dun modr","longbraid","motley garmason","roggo","stockade","thandol span"},rel={"npc:kam-deepfury","subzone:stormwind-stockade","zone:stockade","subzone:dun-modr","quest:303","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Motley Garmason",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=378,ri={"Head of Deepfury"}},src={"The Fury Runs Deep"}}
E["quest:386"] = {t="quest",n="What Comes Around...",z="stockade",s="Guard Berton in Lakeshire is pressing for Targorr the Dread's execution. The Blackrock orc remains in Stormwind Stockade despite his sentence, while political delays keep justice out of reach.",h="Guard Berton in Lakeshire is pressing for Targorr the Dread's execution.",sec={{t="A Butcher Held in Limbo",b="Targorr the Dread earned his name in the Redridge Mountains, where he served as supreme executioner under General Gath'Ilzogg, chieftain of the Blackrock orcs at Stonewatch Keep. Even among the invaders, his cruelty was notorious. He oversaw the torture and execution of many Redridge defenders. After his capture, Stormwind sent him to its high-security prison, the Stormwind Stockade, and condemned him to die for his crimes against the realm.",sp=0},{t="Corruption in High Places",b="An unnamed nobleman in Stormwind's House of Nobles intervened, and Targorr's execution stopped despite his sentence. Guard Berton, stationed in vulnerable Lakeshire, suspects foul play or bribery meant to free the brute. He recruits trusted adventurers to enter the riot-torn prison and carry out the order without bureaucratic interference.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Targorr the Dread?",a="Targorr the Dread is a Blackrock orc who served as supreme executioner under General Gath'Ilzogg in Redridge. He tortured captured human soldiers before his capture and imprisonment in the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"targorr","who is targorr","targorr lore"},it="target"},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind executed Targorr yet?",a="A nobleman in Stormwind delayed Targorr's execution despite his sentence. Guard Berton suspects corruption or foul play meant to spare or exploit the orc warlord.",al={"why is targorr alive","noble stay of execution"}},{q="Who gives the quest What Comes Around...?",a="Guard Berton gives it. He is stationed in Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, where he guards the town against Blackrock orc incursions.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Targorr the Dread be found?",a="Targorr is held in the Stormwind Stockade, in Stormwind City's canal district. He is usually found in a cell in the prison's central cell block.",al={"targorr location","where is targorr"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is General Gath'Ilzogg?",a="General Gath'Ilzogg commands the Blackrock orcs occupying Stonewatch Keep in eastern Redridge. Targorr served under him as executioner.",al={"gath'ilzogg","blackrock general redridge"},it="people"},{q="Why does Guard Berton take matters into his own hands?",a="Berton saw Redridge soldiers suffer and die under Targorr's blades. Disgusted that Stormwind politicians are treating a ruthless murderer as a political pawn, he bypasses official channels to secure justice.",al={"berton motive","why bypass nobles"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Guard Berton want the Head of Targorr?",a="Guard Berton requires Targorr's severed head as undeniable proof that the Blackrock executioner is dead. With a corrupt or meddling noble halting Targorr's lawful execution, Berton cannot rely on official prison reports or bureaucratic word of mouth. Bringing the head back to Lakeshire confirms that justice was served outside the political games of Stormwind.",al={"Head of Targorr purpose","why collect Head of Targorr","what is Targorrs head for"},it="item",add="98ed3ebd"},{q="Why does Guard Berton need an adventurer instead of handling it himself?",a="Guard Berton is stationed out in Lakeshire defending Redridge, bound by military duty and chain of command. He cannot abandon his post or openly enter the Stockade to execute a prisoner whose sentence was officially stayed by Stormwind nobility. An independent adventurer can slip into the prison, bypass political red tape, and carry out the deed without implicating the town guard.",al={"why send me for Targorr","why doesnt Berton kill Targorr","why berton needs me"},it="why_me",add="8d124546"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, this reveals the divide between frontier garrisons like Lakeshire and the self-serving politics of Stormwind's noble courts.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you can settle personal debts for the atrocities Targorr committed against Redridge town guards and militia during the Blackrock invasion.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face the conflict between written law and moral justice when you bypass a corrupt legal delay to punish an unrepentant torturer."},kw={"berton","blackrock","executioner","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","redridge","stockade","targorr"},rel={"npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:guard-berton","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Guard Berton",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=386,ri={"Head of Targorr"}},src={"What Comes Around..."}}
E["quest:387"] = {t="quest",n="Quell The Uprising",z="stockade",s="Warden Thelwater calls for help as the Stockade erupts in riot beneath Stormwind. Defias prisoners have seized the cell blocks, and he wants the uprising crushed before the city's leaders learn how badly the prison has failed.",h="Warden Thelwater calls for help as the Stockade erupts in riot beneath Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Prison Lost to Its Inmates",b="The Stockade holds criminals, conspirators, and outlaws who threaten the Kingdom of Stormwind. Imprisoned Defias operatives have launched a sudden, violent uprising and taken the cell blocks from the guards. Armed felons crowd the corridors, and the usual order has broken down. The guards now depend on visiting champions to fight through the riot and retake the prison.",sp=0},{t="Desperation and Cover-Up",b="Warden Thelwater orders Defias prisoners killed on sight out of desperation and fear for his position. He suspects foul play behind the coordinated mutiny. If the House of Nobles or the wider nobility learns the Stockade is out of control, he fears he will lose his post. Thelwater hopes a death sentence for insurgency will break the inmates' resolve and crush the rebellion before word passes the canal gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Warden Thelwater asking adventurers to put down the riot?",a="The guards have lost control of the Stockade's interior cells to rioting Defias inmates. Warden Thelwater fears losing his position if Stormwind's leaders learn the full scale of the disaster, so he hires capable mercenaries to kill the ringleaders and restore control quickly.",al={"why hire adventurers","thelwater motivation","why the stockade quest"},it="why_me"},{q="Who are the inmates rioting in the Stockade?",a="Captured Defias Brotherhood members form the heart of the uprising. They include common prisoners, hardened convicts, and organized insurgents, locked away while the brotherhood waged its secret war across Westfall and Elwynn Forest.",al={"who is rioting","defias prisoners stockade","who broke out"},it="target"},{q="Does Thelwater believe the riot was an inside job?",a="Yes. Warden Thelwater suspects foul play and believes a revolt this sudden and complete could not happen by chance, without outside interference or compromised security within the city.",al={"was it treason","foul play stockade","inside job prison"}},{q="Where does this uprising take place?",a="The uprising takes place inside The Stockade, a subterranean maximum-security dungeon along the canals in Stormwind City's Mage Quarter.",al={"where is the stockade","stockade entrance","prison location"},it="place"},{q="What happens after these Defias rioters are killed?",a="Killing the rioters weakens the mutineers, but Warden Thelwater admits when you return that the crisis runs deeper than a simple scuffle. Further strikes against high-profile leaders deeper in the cells are needed.",al={"does the prison get safe","after quell the uprising"},it="next_step"},{q="Is lethal force authorized against all escaped convicts?",a="Warden Thelwater declares immediate death the penalty for active insurgency during the takeover. He orders champions to execute prisoners, convicts, and insurgents on the spot, hoping to force the survivors into submission.",al={"why kill them","punishment for insurgency","is killing prisoners legal"}},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater want the uprising quelled?",a="Warden Thelwater is desperate to restore order before city authorities realize just how completely he has lost control. If word reaches the rest of Stormwind that the Stockade is entirely overrun by rioting Defias inmates, he risks losing his position and livelihood. Beyond saving his own job, he fears the violent uprising will spill out of the prison and directly threaten the citizens of Stormwind.",al={"why does thelwater want this done","thelwater motive quell the uprising","why does the warden want them killed"},it="motive",add="2ef5cefa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Stockade rebellion rages beneath Stormwind's streets, a grave security failure at the heart of the Alliance's primary kingdom.",["race:Human"]="Many Defias inmates in the cells are former kingdom stonemasons and common folk driven to rebel. Their bloody riot is a painful civil conflict for Stormwind's people.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, restoring order beneath the city tests the line between righteous justice and desperate, lethal retribution against rebellious citizens."},kw={"convicts","defias","insurgents","quell the uprising","stockade","stormwind","uprising","warden thelwater"},rel={"zone:stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Warden Thelwater",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=387},src={"Quell The Uprising"}}
E["quest:388"] = {t="quest",n="The Color of Blood",z="stockade",s="Nikova Raskol grieves for Mac, her young grandson, killed inside Stormwind City's prison. Anger consumes her, and she sends adventurers into The Stockade to take the Defias gang's red bandanas in retribution.",h="Nikova Raskol grieves for Mac, her young grandson, killed inside Stormwind City's prison.",sec={{t="A Boy on the Prison Wall",b="Mac Raskol was fourteen when he took up arms as a guard in The Stockade. Stormwind's regular soldiers had been sent to distant fronts, leaving local defense to volunteers and the city's youth. Mac watched hardened criminals and mutinous members of the Defias Brotherhood in a place far more dangerous than his experience could prepare him for.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Defiance",b="The Defias inmates tore apart their wool prison blankets and made red bandanas from the scraps. The colors marked their loyalty to the Brotherhood, even behind prison walls. When Mac rebuked them and tried to enforce discipline, the prisoners stabbed him in the back. He died on the stone floor.",sp=0},{t="Grief and Vengeance",b="Nikova Raskol turns from official channels to cold revenge after Mac's pointless death. She sends you into The Stockade to quell the rioting prisoners and bring back ten of their cherished red bandanas. Dyed the color of her grandson's spilled blood, the tokens offer a broken family a grim sense of closure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nikova Raskol?",a="Nikova Raskol is an elderly Stormwind City resident whose fourteen-year-old grandson, Mac, was recently killed while guarding The Stockade.",al={"nikova raskol","quest giver","who gives color of blood"},it="identity"},{q="Why was a fourteen-year-old guarding dangerous prisoners?",a="Stormwind sent much of its regular military to distant fronts, so volunteers and young people filled local defenses, including guard posts in The Stockade.",al={"why was mac a guard","mac age","child guard"},it="history"},{q="Why do the Defias prisoners wear red wool bandanas?",a="Defias prisoners made red bandanas from their wool prison blankets to mark their loyalty to the Brotherhood while behind bars.",al={"why red bandanas","wool bandanas lore","defias red scarves"},it="origin"},{q="How did Mac Raskol die?",a="Mac caught the prisoners tearing their wool blankets to make Defias bandanas and reprimanded them. They stabbed the fourteen-year-old guard in the back.",al={"how did mac die","who killed mac","what happened to mac"},it="conflict"},{q="What does Nikova do with the bandanas?",a="Nikova keeps the bandanas as proof of retribution. She stares at the torn wool tokens and grieves her grandson's senseless death, finding peace in knowing his killers faced justice.",al={"what happens to the bandanas","nikova bandanas"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You enter The Stockade, Stormwind City's high-security prison in the canal district, where Defias prisoners are in open revolt.",al={"where do i get the bandanas","color of blood location"},it="place"},{q="Why does Nikova Raskol want this done?",a="Nikova is consumed by grief and a desire for vengeance. Her fourteen-year-old grandson, Mac, stepped up to serve as a guard in the Stockade when the regular army was deployed to the front lines. When Mac caught Defias inmates shredding their wool blankets to fashion gang colors, he reprimanded them, and they stabbed him in the back. Claiming the Defias bandanas is her way of seeking justice and bloody retribution for Mac's senseless murder.",al={"why does nikova want revenge","nikova raskol motive","why kill the defias in the stockade"},it="motive",add="04f6762b"},{q="Who are you fighting in the Stockade for this quest?",a="You are sent against the Defias inmates rioting within the Stockade. These thieves, brigands, and rebel stonemasons were imprisoned beneath Stormwind for their violent insurrection against the crown. Left lightly guarded after the city garrison marched off to distant fronts, the convicts rose up, seized control of the prison cells, and brutally butchered the young militia members holding watch over them.",al={"who has the red wool bandanas","who are you sent against","the color of blood targets"},it="target",add="c39081cf"},{q="Why does Nikova ask an adventurer instead of the city guards?",a="Stormwind's regular military forces were dispatched to distant fronts, leaving the city strapped for experienced soldiers. The local militia and inexperienced conscripts—like young Mac Raskol—were already overwhelmed when the prisoners revolted, losing control of the Stockade entirely. With the remaining city watch stretched thin securing the streets outside the prison, Nikova must turn to capable, independent adventurers willing to storm the cells and exact her revenge.",al={"why doesn't the stormwind guard handle it","why me color of blood","why does nikova need you"},it="why_me",add="bfcf62d8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Mac Raskol's death shows the strain on Stormwind's home defense and the dire cost of sending seasoned soldiers far from the capital.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share Stormwind's burden from Defias violence in the surrounding farmlands and within the city walls."},kw={"color of blood","defias brotherhood","mac raskol","nikova raskol","red wool bandana","stockade","stormwind"},rel={"zone:stockade","npc:nikova-raskol","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Nikova Raskol",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=388,ri={"Red Wool Bandana"}},src={"The Color of Blood"}}
E["quest:391"] = {t="quest",n="The Stockade Riots",z="stockade",s="At Stormwind's prison gates, Warden Thelwater sends you into the Stockade Riots to prove your loyalty to the city guards. The uprising has seized the prison, and he orders you to find and execute its ringleader, Bazil Thredd.",h="At Stormwind's prison gates, Warden Thelwater sends you into the Stockade Riots to prove your loyalty to the...",sec={{t="Blood on the Stone",b="Deep beneath the Mage Quarter's cobblestones, the Stockade has fallen into lawlessness. Criminals, Defias insurgents, and violent cutthroats have broken containment and seized the cell blocks, making the prison an impenetrable war zone. Warden Thelwater and his guards cling desperately to the entrance, unable to push inside and restore order by ordinary means.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Trust",b="Warden Thelwater distrusts anyone asking after Bazil Thredd, so he demands proof of your allegiance. He orders you through the riot-torn cell blocks to slay Thredd in his cell and return with the rebel leader's severed head. Only by killing the uprising's figurehead can an outsider show they are not secretly allied with the rebellion.",sp=1},{t="A Severed Thread",b="Bazil Thredd leads the riot, and his death deals the uprising's organization a decisive blow. It also silences any direct answers he might have given about the conspiracy gripping Stormwind. When Warden Thelwater sees Thredd's head, he is surprised and admits the prison may become manageable again. He also offers clues about Thredd's secret contacts before the insurrection.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Stockade Riots?",a="Warden Thelwater gives it just inside the Stockade's entrance tunnel in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"who gives the stockade riots","stockade riots quest giver","where to start stockade riots"},gp=true},{q="What do I need to do to complete the quest?",a="You must enter the prison dungeon, find ringleader Bazil Thredd in the eastern cell block, kill him, and return his severed head to Warden Thelwater.",al={"stockade riots objective","how to beat stockade riots"},gp=true},{q="Where is Bazil Thredd located inside the Stockade?",a="From the entrance, follow the northern corridor to the T-intersection, then take the eastern cell block. Bazil Thredd is in the center cell of a three-room chamber guarded by the ogre Hamhock.",al={"where is thredd","bazil thredd location","how to find thredd"},gp=true},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater want Bazil Thredd dead?",a="Bazil Thredd is the uprising's primary ringleader. Warden Thelwater believes killing him is the only way for the guards to regain control of the rioting cell blocks, and it also tests whether you are secretly working with the rebels.",al={"why kill thredd","why thelwater wants thredd dead"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after completing The Stockade Riots?",a="After you bring back Thredd's head, Warden Thelwater sends you to investigate a mysterious figure who visited the prison before the riot. The next stage is called The Curious Visitor.",al={"stockade riots follow up","what comes after stockade riots"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can Horde players obtain this quest?",a="No. The Stockade is a dungeon deep inside Stormwind, the Alliance capital, so Horde players cannot obtain this.",al={"is stockade riots alliance only","horde stockade riots"},gp=true},{q="What is the Head of Bazil Thredd for?",a="Warden Thelwater demands the severed head of Bazil Thredd as absolute proof of his demise and of your allegiance. Deeply suspicious of anyone seeking an audience with the riot leader, Thelwater makes it clear that returning with Thredd's head is the only way you walk out of the prison without being branded a traitor and executed alongside the rebellious convicts.",al={"head of bazil thredd use","why sever thredd head","bazil thredd head"},it="item",add="324bbcda"},{q="Who is Bazil Thredd, and why is he in the Stockade?",a="Bazil Thredd is a high-ranking member of the Defias Brotherhood imprisoned beneath the streets of Stormwind. Orchestrating unrest from within the prison walls, Thredd has organized the inmates into an open, armed uprising, seizing control of cell blocks and holding the facility hostage against the warden's guards.",al={"who is bazil thredd","bazil thredd backstory","why is thredd imprisoned"},it="target",add="3413d34a"},{q="Why does Warden Thelwater send you instead of his own guards?",a="The Stockade is engulfed in total revolt, and the warden's beleaguered guards are stretched thin trying to contain the violent outbreak at the entrance. Because you arrived specifically seeking to speak with Thredd, Thelwater doubts your loyalty; sending you into the fray risks nothing for the garrison while offering a simple test—either you cut down the ringleader to prove your innocence, or you die alongside the rioters.",al={"why send me into the stockade","why doesnt thelwater send guards","why me stockade riots"},it="why_me",add="16764756"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="A full-scale revolt beneath the Mage Quarter threatens Stormwind's stability while the King remains missing and the kingdom is stretched thin.",["race:Human"]="Many rioters are Defias operatives and disgruntled stonemasons who turned against their kingdom after the reconstruction dispute.",["class:Rogue"]="Infiltrating the riot shows how far the Defias Brotherhood's clandestine underground network can go when it loses all restraint."},kw={"bazil thredd","defias","hamhock","stockade riots","stormwind","the stockade","warden thelwater"},rel={"quest:389","zone:stockade","npc:warden-thelwater","npc:hamhock","quest:392"},m={start="Warden Thelwater",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=391,ri={"Head of Bazil Thredd"}},src={"The Stockade Riots"}}
E["zone:stockade"] = {t="dungeon",n="The Stockade",z="stockade",s="The Stockade holds dangerous prisoners beneath Stormwind's canal district near the Mage Quarter. Built as a high-security prison for cutthroats, political insurgents, and captured enemies of state, it has fallen into violent anarchy. Warden Thelwater is forced back to the entrance, seeking help to crush the riot before it reaches the capital.",h="The Stockade holds dangerous prisoners beneath Stormwind's canal district near the Mage Quarter.",sec={{t="A Prison Under Siege",b="Beneath Stormwind's canals, the Stockade has become a war zone. When the regular army marched to distant fronts, the understaffed prison relied on inexperienced youths, including fourteen-year-old recruits, to keep order. They failed. The inmates launched a bloody, coordinated rebellion, tore their wool blankets into gang scarves, and cut down the remaining guards. Warden Thelwater barely holds the entrance, while convicts control the cells, hallways, and holding blocks.",sp=0},{t="Nobles and Assassins",b="The riot exposed Stormwind's political dealings. Outside territories had grown frustrated with the House of Nobles halting executions for its own leverage. Redridge guard Berton wanted the captured orc Targorr the Dread executed for atrocities, but the nobles froze his sentence. Darkshire councilman Millstipe saw grave robber Dextren Ward spared the gallows despite desecrating graves for the necromancer Morbent Fel. The dwarves of Dun Modr also demanded the death of Dark Iron saboteur Kam Deepfury. With the Stockade in chaos, local authorities quietly hired adventurers to carry out the executions the capital's courts refused to enforce.",sp=1,bt={"q303.3"}},{t="The Mastermind and the Rioters",b="Bazil Thredd, a cunning felon tied to the Defias Brotherhood, orchestrated the uprising from his cell. Bruegal Ironknuckle, a dangerous dwarven brawler, is among the rioters. He is one of several hardened convicts adventurers may meet while helping Thelwater reclaim the prison.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Stockade in open rebellion?",a="The Defias Brotherhood orchestrated a prison-wide riot while the facility was severely understaffed. With the Stormwind Army deployed to distant battlefronts, teenage volunteers guarded hardened killers. The convicts ambushed the staff, seized weapons, and drove Warden Thelwater out of the cellblocks.",al={"why riot","what happened in stockades","stockades riot cause"},it="history"},{q="Who is running the uprising inside?",a="Bazil Thredd, an influential Defias felon incarcerated in the eastern cellblock, masterminded the revolt. Other dangerous prisoners include Bruegal Ironknuckle, Hamhock, and Kam Deepfury.",al={"stockades boss","who leads the riot","who runs stockades"},it="leader"},{q="Why are prisoners like Targorr and Dextren Ward still alive?",a="Both were condemned to death, but corrupt politicians in the House of Nobles placed bureaucratic holds on their executions to use the prisoners as political leverage. This interference outraged allies in Lakeshire and Darkshire, who sent adventurers to eliminate them during the chaos.",al={"why wasn't targorr executed","dextren ward court","house of nobles corruption"},it="threat"},{q="What does defeating Bruegal Ironknuckle mean for the prison?",a="Bruegal Ironknuckle is a dangerous dwarven brawler among the rioters. Defeating him removes one threat while adventurers work to put down the uprising.",al={"bruegal ironknuckle lore","kill bruegal","who is bruegal"},it="threat"},{q="Why are there Dark Iron dwarves and orcs inside a human jail?",a="The Stockade is a maximum-security holding pen for high-value prisoners of war. Targorr the Dread led Blackrock orc attacks in Redridge, while Kam Deepfury sabotaged the Wetlands for the Dark Iron clan. Both were captured and transferred to the capital.",al={"why dark irons here","kam deepfury lore","targorr stockades"},it="residents"},{q="Can Horde players enter the Stockade?",a="Yes, but entering is exceptionally hazardous. The dungeon portal sits inside Stormwind City near the Mage Quarter canals. Horde infiltrators must sneak past the city guards and the capital's defenders to reach it.",al={"can horde do stockades","horde in stormwind prison"},gp=true},{q="What is the Stockade?",a="The Stockade is Stormwind's high-security prison complex, built beneath the canal district of the capital. It serves as holding pens for petty thieves, cutthroats, political insurgents, and high-profile enemies of the kingdom awaiting judgment.",al={"what is stormwind stockade","stockade prison","stormwind jail"},it="place",add="07af5e0b",nx={8}},{q="Is the Stockade just for Defias?",a="No. While the Defias Brotherhood makes up the core of the uprising, the cells hold petty thieves, grave-robbers like Dextren Ward, captured Blackrock orcs like Targorr the Dread, and even Dark Iron saboteurs like Kam Deepfury.",al={"is stockade only defias","who is in stockade","are all prisoners defias"},it="place",add="2fc364a6"},{q="Why are there so many Defias locked up in here?",a="Stormwind's authorities have captured Brotherhood operatives across Westfall, Elwynn Forest, and the city itself. Rather than executing them outright, the crown hauled them into the Stockade, concentrating a volatile network of insurgents right under the city's floorboards.",al={"why so many defias here","why defias in stockade","defias brotherhood prisoners"},it="threat",add="0d433487"},{q="Who's in charge of this prison?",a="Warden Thelwater presides over the facility. When the uprising broke out, his guards were overwhelmed and driven from the holding blocks. Thelwater barely held the entryway, leaving him desperately recruiting capable adventurers to take back the corridors.",al={"who runs stockade","stockade warden","warden thelwater"},it="in_charge",add="e96a18b2",nx={11}},{q="Why can't Warden Thelwater's guards handle the riot?",a="The prison guard was already stretched remarkably thin, even resorting to volunteers as young as fourteen to watch dangerous convicts. When the Defias banded together and attacked, the staff was caught completely off guard, slaughtered, or forced to flee into the entrance hall.",al={"why cant guards stop riot","where are prison guards","guards stockade"},it="in_charge",add="06cbacdc"},{q="Why is Stormwind sending me in instead of the army?",a="Much of Stormwind's military is deployed to distant fronts, and corrupt bureaucracy in the House of Nobles paralyzes swift municipal action. Furthermore, city officials are desperate to keep the riot a secret to avoid outright panic in the streets.",al={"why send adventurers","why not the army stockade","where is stormwind army"},it="why_me",add="7c158547",nx={13}},{q="Do the guards outside know what's going on inside?",a="The guards contain the rioters at the dungeon threshold, and Warden Thelwater seeks help to restore order inside. City officials keep the disturbance quiet to avoid alarming ordinary citizens.",al={"do outside guards know","does stormwind know riot","stockade secret"},it="why_me",add="a2006c52"},{q="What's the difference between the prisoners, convicts and insurgents in here?",a="The inmates range from common crooks and cutpurses swept off the streets to convicted felons and hardline Defias insurgents. While ordinary convicts took the chance to riot and pillage, the insurgents actively take orders from Bazil Thredd to overthrow the prison.",al={"convicts insurgents prisoners","stockade enemy types","who are the inmates"},it="threat",add="b1798127"},{q="How did the inmates get weapons and organize?",a="The uprising was meticulously plotted by Defias ringleader Bazil Thredd. Under his direction, prisoners tore their wool blankets into red gang scarves, jumped understaffed guards, stole their weapons and keys, and methodically freed cells across every wing.",al={"how did prisoners get weapons","how did defias organize","who armed the prisoners"},it="history",add="378bbf14"},{q="Why put a prison right under the city?",a="The prison complex lies beneath Stormwind's canals. Its original placement is not explained.",al={"why prison under stormwind","stockade location why","prison under canals"},it="place",add="855deb71"},{q="How did I end up in The Stockade?",a="You walked through the heavy iron doors off the northern canals in Stormwind City. A massive riot broke out beneath the streets, and Warden Thelwater's remaining guards were forced back to the threshold, leaving the convicts in control. Desperate to keep the chaos hidden from the citizens above, the warden enlisted able-bodied adventurers to march straight down into the cellblocks and retake the facility by force.",al={"how did i get here","why did i come here","how did i enter the stockade"},it="arrival",add="caa2e4bf"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in The Stockade?",a="Your primary mission is to break the rebellion and put an end to its ringleader, the Defias mastermind Bazil Thredd. However, allies across the kingdom have seized this moment of chaos to settle overdue debts: Darkshire seeks retribution against the grave-robber Dextren Ward, Lakeshire wants the ruthless orc Targorr the Dread slain, and Ironforge demands the head of the saboteur Kam Deepfury.",al={"what is my mission here","what do i do here","why am i here"},it="purpose",add="45edc40e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The rebellion threatens Stormwind's internal security and the heart of the capital. Putting it down preserves that security and honors off-the-books bounties for Redridge, Duskwood, and Ironforge.",["race:Dwarf"]="Kam Deepfury's presence in Stormwind's cells affronts Dun Modr. The Kingdom of Ironforge demands his head to avenge dwarven lives lost in the Wetlands.",["class:Rogue"]="The prison's intricate web of locked iron cells and Defias connections offers unique lockpicking practice and insight into Bazil Thredd's underworld syndicate.",["class:Mage"]="The prison lies on the canal edge of the Mage Quarter, where physical brawlers are vulnerable to slowing spells. The ogre mage Hamhock can unleash Chain Lightning."},kw={"bazil thredd","bruegal ironknuckle","canals","defias","dextren ward","hamhock","kam deepfury","riot","stockade","stormwind","targorr","warden thelwater"},rel={"npc:warden-thelwater","npc:bruegal-ironknuckle","npc:kam-deepfury","npc:targorr-the-dread","npc:dextren-ward","quest:391","quest:389"},m={levels="24-32"},src={"Stormwind Stockade (Classic)","Stormwind Stockade"}}
